<details><summary>Statistical caution</summary>
The construction concerns unrestricted answer functions. Additional assumptions can support statistical inference, and checkable certificates can verify particular claims. Without such structure, finite coordinate observations never uniquely determine an infinite bitstream. Background on the [halting problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halting_problem) explains why negative halting answers are especially difficult to certify.
</details>

## Forgetting as a quotient

Finite memory faces the dual problem: it cannot preserve every distinction among an infinite collection of finite streams. Targeted deletion groups streams by the retained subsequence.

{{algorithm:2}}

{{visualization:2}}

{{demo:2}}

<details><summary>Reveal the algebraic structure</summary>
A compositional memory satisfies $m(xy)=m(x)m(y)$. Equality of memories is therefore compatible with concatenation and defines a monoid congruence. The quotient by that relation is isomorphic to the reachable memory representations; streams sent to the identity form a submonoid. For general background, see [quotient structures](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quotient_(universal_algebra)).
</details>

## Synthesis

Finite memory must merge some histories. Universal exact oracle storage must merge none of the infinitely many answer streams. The mathematical boundary is distinguishability: oracle evaluation is simple, while exact acquisition and preservation of arbitrary infinite information carries the exceptional premise.
